# Android ↔ web tester

Canonical doc: [`docs/ANDROID_WEB_TEST.md`](docs/ANDROID_WEB_TEST.md).

- **`relay-runtime`** owns the **test APK** (`android-demo/`) and **web test app** (`examples/wasm-test/`). Prove runtime changes there first.
- **`relay-client-android`** is the product RelayClient (**Rust** `librelay_runtime.so`, not npm). Not the first harness.
- `./scripts/build-install-demo.sh` then `./scripts/test-wasm.sh`. Compare Android to web. Web is the CSS standard; Android applies `props.style` to native views.
- Same client hooks on both hosts. Skip Windows/macOS native UI; desktop is web.

**When you change Android testing:** update `docs/ANDROID_WEB_TEST.md` in the same change (Current state, Next steps, Progress log). See that file’s **Agent instructions**.
